# Current desktop screenshots and README walkthrough GIFs
Workstream-ID: lea-16
GitHub-Issue: https://github.com/Zanark/LinkedIn-EasyApply-Automaton/issues/16
Publication: PUBLIC_SAFE_PROJECTION
Source-record: Reviewed current desktop documentation and offline media scope
Status: DONE
Milestone: Make current desktop controls understandable through safe visual examples
Dependencies: lea-15

## Purpose
Refresh the README's desktop screenshots and add short run-setup and read-only
tutorial GIFs from current source. Use independent fictional fixtures, not
personal setup, browser authentication, runtime history or desktop recordings.
This bounded documentation task does not authorize another source push or release.

## Tasks
- [x] Inspect current documentation, capture tooling, controls and private-state boundaries.
- [x] Extend the existing capture tool with actual GUI transitions and explicit widget cleanup.
- [x] Refresh desktop screenshots, including every customization tab.
- [x] Generate and inspect run-control and tutorial walkthrough GIFs.
- [x] Embed media with captions, static alternatives and reproducible prerequisites.
- [x] Verify focused behavior, animation integrity and preservation of original inputs/preferences.
- [x] Preview scoped tracking and verify the issue, Project status and durable backlink.

## Acceptance criteria
- [x] Desktop screenshots show the current version and readable text in both existing themes.
- [x] Run GIF shows action-specific controls and all four customization tabs.
- [x] Tutorial GIF shows Back/Next and direct topic selection without changing its parent.
- [x] Animations contain real UI transitions, readable holds and a looping GIF encoding.
- [x] Public images contain only fictional data and paths; original setup remains untouched.
- [x] Captures execute no automation, copy no clipboard command and create no run presets.
- [x] README retains static alternatives with meaningful captions and alt text.
- [x] Capture tooling uses development-only dependencies and destroys its owned Qt widgets.
- [x] Tracking preserves all earlier identities, baselines and original review gaps.
- [x] Local technical completion is distinguished from publication and human/live qualification.

## Completion evidence
Regenerated thirteen current-source desktop PNGs, including Search, Limits,
Browser and Behavior, both themes and the smaller window. Tools now displays
0.2.1 and fictional demo locations rather than checkout-specific paths.
The run walkthrough contains nine frames, lasts 17.8 seconds and is 980709 bytes;
the tutorial contains seven frames, lasts 14.2 seconds and is 364065 bytes.
Both loop, have 1.8-2.8 second holds and decode completely. Cropping away captions
verified nine distinct run UI states and six tutorial UI states.

Assistant visual review covered all thirteen PNGs and eight representative
GIF states through two contact sheets, plus full-size Tools, Configuration and
the run Limits frame. This is sampled visual inspection, not a claim of watching
the complete animations or receiving human aesthetic acceptance.
All twenty-two README/GUI image references resolve with nonempty alt text;
all fifteen GUI assets appear in the README. Captions explain fictional state,
non-execution boundaries and static alternatives. The legacy dashboard image
is unchanged; no new dashboard or installed-release qualification is claimed.

The thirty-five focused window/tutorial cases passed with process exit zero,
including actual UI-area transitions, preserved parent state and injected GIF
encoding failure cleanup. Scoped Ruff and Black passed. Current native preference
values and registry timestamp, selected original-input size/mtime metadata,
all fifteen earlier mapping objects and source HEAD were preserved. This is
metadata preservation, not a full private-content hash comparison.
Captures use temporary explicit UserScope/SystemScope INI paths and owned widgets,
never Start, Copy command, Save or a launcher. Pillow is declared in development
extras only and was already installed. No run preset, dependency installation,
live action, source commit/push or new release occurred.

Initial scoped synchronization independently verified issue #16, one In Progress
Project item and the persistent backlink; all fifteen prior issues/items,
timestamps, source files and original #2/#9 OPEN/In review gaps were unchanged.
Completion reconciliation and settlement receipts belong in the excluded
index/ledger rather than repeatedly changing this managed evidence.

